    "    "## Natural Language Processing (Fall 2026)\n",
    "# Text Classification with Naive Bayes\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**Author:** Ahmed ElSawy  \n",
    "**Date:** October 2026  \n",
    "**Topic:** Bag-of-Words & Multinomial Naive Bayes Text Classification from Scratch vs. Scikit-Learn\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Project Overview & Objectives\n",
    "The goal of this assignment is to develop an end-to-end Natural Language Processing (NLP) pipeline for multi-class text categorization using the **Multinomial Naive Bayes** algorithm.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key project milestones:\n",
    "1. **Text Preprocessing:** Lowercasing, noise & punctuation removal, tokenization, stop word filtering, and length normalization.\n",
    "2. **Train/Test Splitting:** Stratified split with a fixed random seed (`random_state=42`) to prevent data leakage and ensure reproducibility.\n",
    "3. **Vocabulary Construction:** Strictly building the feature dictionary from the training partition only.\n",
    "4. **Bag-of-Words (BoW) Vectorization:** Custom transformation mapping tokenized documents to feature count vectors.\n",
    "5. **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) & Visualizations:**\n",
    "   - Class distribution bar charts (Train vs. Test).\n",
    "   - Sentence length distribution bar charts (character & word counts).\n",
    "   - Word frequency bar charts (corpus-wide & class-specific).\n",
    "   - High-resolution Word Clouds for each of the four categories.\n",
    "6. **From-Scratch Naive Bayes Classifier:** Custom Python class implementing Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE), Laplace (add-1) smoothing, and log-space inference without external ML libraries.\n",
    "7. **Scikit-Learn Naive Bayes Classifier:** Training `MultinomialNB` on identical BoW representations to validate our manual mathematical implementation.\n",
    "8. **Comprehensive Evaluation:**\n",
    "   - Train and test set accuracy reporting.\n",
    "   - Confusion matrix heatmaps annotated with counts.\n",
    "   - Per-class Precision, Recall, and F1-score computation and comparison.\n",
    "   - Qualitative feature importance and error analysis."
   ]
  },
