    "---\n",
    "## 2. Text Preprocessing Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "Text preprocessing converts unstructured raw strings into normalized token sequences. Our preprocessing pipeline consists of:\n",
    "1. **Lowercasing:** Eliminates case sensitivity so that words like `\"Football\"` and `\"football\"` share the same token identity.\n",
    "2. **Noise and Punctuation Removal:** Uses regular expressions (`[^a-z\\s]`) to remove digits, punctuation, and special symbols.\n",
    "3. **Tokenization:** Splits whitespace-separated text into distinct word tokens.\n",
    "4. **Stop Word Removal:** Filters out high-frequency function words (e.g., `'the'`, `'is'`, `'at'`, `'which'`) using standard English stop words. Stop words carry little category-specific semantic signal and inflate vocabulary size.\n",
    "5. **Length Filtering:** Retains tokens with length $\\ge 2$ to discard residual single-character artifacts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "bff1f8e2",
   "metadata": {
